Cell["\<\
In convention I, the Bloch phase is attached to the full displacement between \
orbitals. Convention II moves the intracell orbital-center phases into the \
basis states.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"395f4e95-c509-4fd1-9747-ec06b1159826"],

Cell["\<\
Initialize the model first so that the fractional orbital centers are known, \
or supply them with \"wcc\". An explicit list must follow the row and column \
order of H, and lets symhamII convert a user-supplied Hamiltonian without \
relying on the current init session. The transformation changes the matrix \
phases but not the energy spectrum.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"8340429f-358f-445c-9f17-8a8f732010c9"],

Cell[BoxData[GridBox[{
   {Cell["      ", "TableRowIcon",ExpressionUUID->
     "5d1e38c0-747f-4c35-a775-d38f9337e62e"], "\"\<wcc\>\"", "None", 
    Cell["\<\
None uses the orbital centers prepared by init. An explicit list supplies one \
fractional center per Hamiltonian orbital in the same order as the rows and \
columns of H.\
\>", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"f4945624-b755-4dce-835e-eb7497e329c3"]}
  },
  GridBoxAlignment->{"Columns" -> {{Left}}},
  GridBoxDividers->{"Rows" -> {{False}}},
  GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {
      Offset[0.27999999999999997`], {
       Offset[0.7]}, 
      Offset[0.27999999999999997`]}, "Rows" -> {
      Offset[0.2], {
